# Tooling visibility, independent of git.
#
# .gitignore keeps these out of commits. This file re-exposes them to
# ripgrep-based search and file-listing tools, which honor .ignore ahead of
# .gitignore. Nothing here affects what git tracks.
#
# Not negated on purpose:
#   db/              live PostgreSQL cluster, owned by postgres and unreadable
#                    (negating it only produces "Permission denied" noise)
#   __pycache__/     build artifacts, no reason to search
#   server/bin/*     compiled binaries
#   ref/*.tar.gz     the extracted trees next to them are what you want
#
# ref/ is re-exposed: it holds the Eventdisplay reference implementation, and
# grepping it is how the camera-frame convention was settled. rg skips the
# binaries in it on its own.

!*.bin
!*.fits
!*.log
!server/cmd/server/log.txt
!server/cmd/server/server
!server/cmd/send_command/send_command
!server/bin/*
!fadc/src/server_unified.c
!fadc/src/clbt1.c
!fadc/testfadc/
!ref/
ref/*.tar.gz